      "text": "To find the number of students who did not receive an A in any of the two courses, we can use the principle of inclusion-exclusion.\n\n1. Total number of students: 30\n2. Number of students who received an A in history (H): 7\n3. Number of students who received an A in math (M): 13\n4. Number of students who received an A in both history and math: 4\n\nUsing the principle of inclusion-exclusion, we can find the number of students who received an A in either history or math or both:\n\n\\[ \\text{Number of students who received an A in either history or math or both} = 7 + 13 - 4 = 16 \\]\n\nNext, to find the number of students who did not get an A in either course, we subtract the number of students who received an A in either course from the total number of students:\n\n\\[ \\text{Number of students who did not get an A in either course} = 30 - 16 = 14 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this by writing the Python code.\n```python\n# Given values\ntotal_students = 30\nA_in_history = 7\nA_in_math = 13\nA_in_both = 4\n\n# Using the principle of inclusion-exclusion\nA_in_either_or_both = A_in_history + A_in_math - A_in_both\n\n# Number of students who did not get an A in either course\nstudents_no_A = total_students - A_in_either_or_both\nprint(students_no_A)\n```\n```output\n14\n```\nThe number of students who did not receive an A in any of the two courses is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).",
